course: dictionary
lesson: 8479
title: Samoan: a place, a person, a language
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Samoan can describe something, name a person, or name a language. Context tells you which one. «In Auckland, Koa's grandad in Samoa sends voice messages in Samoan» uses it as the name of a language, because you send messages in a language.
explain: Look at the words after the word. «Samoan language» and «Samoan culture» use Samoan to describe something, so it means from or belonging to Samoa. When it stands alone and means a person, it is a noun: a Samoan is someone from Samoa.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Koa understands half, and his mum translates the rest» tells you Koa needs help, so the messages must be in a language he does not fully know. That is the clue that Samoan means the language.
fact: Samoan means from or belonging to Samoa, a group of islands in the Pacific Ocean.
fact: A Samoan is a person from Samoa.
fact: Samoan is also the language spoken in Samoa.
fact: Many Samoans live in New Zealand and Australia, and Samoan is widely spoken in Auckland.
fact: Samoa is in Polynesia, an area of islands in the Pacific.
exercise: «Koa's grandad sends voice messages in Samoan.» What is Samoan in this sentence? | *The language they speak | A kind of food | A type of phone | A town in Auckland
exercise: «Koa's grandad in Samoa» tells us where Koa's grandad lives. Where is Samoa? | A lake in Canada | *A group of islands in the Pacific Ocean | A city in Australia | A mountain in Scotland
exercise: Koa's grandad lives in Samoa. What is a person from Samoa called? | Australian | Aucklander | *Samoan | Scot
test: In «Samoan culture», what does Samoan mean? | *From or belonging to Samoa | A person who speaks two languages | The name of an ocean | A hot drink from the islands
test: «Many Samoans live in New Zealand and Australia.» What does Samoans mean here? | *People from Samoa | Words spoken in a school | Shops that sell food from Auckland | Islands in the Pacific
exam: In «the Samoan language», Samoan means | a holiday in Auckland | *belonging to Samoa | a person from Samoa | a kind of island
